.TH OH-NO-PARENT-CONTROL 1 "September 2026" "Oh No! Parent Control" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oh-no-parent-control \- run the parent-control request station
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oh-no-parent-control
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oh-no-parent-control
starts the full-screen request station used by the dedicated kiosk session.
It normally obtains managed-user information and submits access requests
through the privileged Oh No! Parent Control broker.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Render representative fixture data without contacting privileged services.
.TP
.B \-\-child-overlay
Present the shared request interface for the current child account instead of
showing the kiosk account selector.
.TP
.BI \-\-soundtrack " file"
Play the specified audio file instead of the installed request-station
soundtrack.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/oh-no-parent-control/config.json
Root-owned machine configuration generated during package installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oh-no-parent-control-parent (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Puffy Slippers Tech LLC.
